{"id":"at-smokies","title":"Appalachian Trail through the Smokies","who":"Classic route · the A.T.'s highest section","when":"April–June and September–October","vehicle":"On foot, 5–7 days, shelters (permit needed)","kind":"walk","color":"#15803d","summary":"About 70 miles of the Appalachian Trail along the crest of Great Smoky Mountains National Park, from Fontana Dam over Clingmans Dome (Kuwohi), the trail's highest point at 6,643 ft, to Davenport Gap. Misty ridges, bald meadows, black bears and shelters. Hurricane damage closed the trail north of Davenport Gap in 2025: check the ATC.","sources":[{"label":"ATC: Davenport Gap and I-40 area damage (2025 updates)","url":"https://appalachiantrail.org/trail-updates/davenport-gap-i-40-area-damage/"},{"label":"Friends of the Smokies: ridgerunners on the A.T., 2025","url":"https://friendsofthesmokies.org/blog/ridgerunners-on-appalachian-trail-gsmnp-2025/"}],"approximate":"Main points; the line follows the trail where it was found.","km":90,"bbox":[-83.8053,35.4522,-83.1112,35.7711],"stops":[{"name":"Fontana Dam","place":"Fontana Dam","at":[35.4522,-83.8053],"text":"Across the dam into the park, the \"Fontana Hilton\" shelter behind."},{"name":"Spence Field","place":"Spence Field","at":[35.5642,-83.7375],"text":"A grassy bald with views, under Thunderhead."},{"name":"Clingmans Dome (Kuwohi)","place":"Clingmans Dome","at":[35.5629,-83.4984],"text":"The highest point of the whole A.T., with an observation tower.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Clingmans_Dome_Sevierville_TN.jpg/500px-Clingmans_Dome_Sevierville_TN.jpg","page":"Kuwohi","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clingmans_Dome_Sevierville_TN.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Newfound Gap","place":"Newfound Gap","at":[35.6111,-83.425],"text":"The road across the park, and the halfway point.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Revised_Rockefeller_Memorial_at_Newfound_Gap_IMG_5140.JPG/500px-Revised_Rockefeller_Memorial_at_Newfound_Gap_IMG_5140.JPG","page":"Newfound Gap","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Revised_Rockefeller_Memorial_at_Newfound_Gap_IMG_5140.JPG","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Charlies Bunion","place":"Charlies Bunion","at":[35.6367,-83.3753],"text":"A bare rock outcrop with huge views.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Charlies-bunion-protrusion.jpg/500px-Charlies-bunion-protrusion.jpg","page":"Charlies Bunion","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charlies-bunion-protrusion.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Cosby Knob","place":"Cosby Knob Shelter","at":[35.7389,-83.1814],"text":"Down the long northern ridge.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/View_atop_Cliff_Tops_on_Mount_LeConte%2C_GSMNP%2C_TN.jpg/500px-View_atop_Cliff_Tops_on_Mount_LeConte%2C_GSMNP%2C_TN.jpg","page":"Great Smoky Mountains National Park","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_atop_Cliff_Tops_on_Mount_LeConte%2C_GSMNP%2C_TN.jpg","credit":"AppalachianCentrist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Davenport Gap","place":"Davenport Gap","at":[35.7707,-83.1113],"text":"The park's north end, near I-40; the trail beyond was damaged in 2025.","source":{"label":"ATC trail update","url":"https://appalachiantrail.org/trail-updates/davenport-gap-i-40-area-damage/"}}],"legs":[{"by":"walk","km":14,"line":[[35.4522,-83.8053],[35.5642,-83.7375]]},{"by":"walk","km":26,"line":[[35.5648,-83.7379],[35.5621,-83.7226],[35.5704,-83.6944],[35.566,-83.6439],[35.569,-83.6272],[35.58,-83.6084],[35.5749,-83.5958],[35.5628,-83.5841],[35.5662,-83.5652],[35.5629,-83.4984]]},{"by":"walk","km":12,"line":[[35.5629,-83.4984],[35.5686,-83.4851],[35.5833,-83.4788],[35.5866,-83.4724],[35.5907,-83.4742],[35.5922,-83.4633],[35.6109,-83.4475],[35.6111,-83.425]]},{"by":